          "content": "2 ARITHMETIC EXPRESSIONS"
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.783,
            0.093,
            0.903,
            0.18
          ],
          "content": ""
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.82,
            0.184,
            0.868,
            0.195
          ],
          "content": "0774CH02"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.298,
            0.477,
            0.323
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "2.1 Simple Expressions"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.332,
            0.847,
            0.373
          ],
          "content": "$1 8 \\div 3 .$ . Such phrases are called arithmetic expressions."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.373,
            0.848,
            0.428
          ],
          "content": "Every arithmetic expression has a value which is the number it evaluates to. For example, the value of the expression 13 + 2 is 15. This expression can be read as $^ { \\circ } 1 3$ plus $2 ^ { \\circ }$ or ‘the sum of 13 and $2 ^ { \\circ }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.428,
            0.848,
            0.465
          ],
          "content": "We use the equality sign $\\text{\" }  二  \\text{\" }$ to denote the relationship between an arithmetic expression and its value. For example:"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.441,
            0.468,
            0.556,
            0.488
          ],
          "content": "13 \\pm 2 = 15.",
          "image_source": "images/page_0_equation_7.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.503,
            0.848,
            0.561
          ],
          "content": "? **Example 1:** Mallika spends ₹25 every day for lunch at school. Write the expression for the total amount she spends on lunch in a week from Monday to Friday."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.566,
            0.648,
            0.604
          ],
          "content": "The expression for the total amount is 5 × 25. $5 \\times 2 5$ is $^ { \\circ } 5$ times $2 5 ^ { \\circ }$ or “the product of 5 and $2 5 ^ { \\circ }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.614,
            0.848,
            0.671
          ],
          "content": "Different expressions can have the same value. Here are multiple ways to express the number 12, using two numbers and any of the four operations +, – , × and ÷:"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.367,
            0.674,
            0.628,
            0.695
          ],
          "content": "10+2,15-3,3\\times4,24\\div2.",
          "image_source": "images/page_0_equation_11.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.708,
            0.847,
            0.749
          ],
          "content": "？ Choose your favourite number and write as many expressions as you can having that value."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.767,
            0.447,
            0.79
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Comparing Expressions"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.799,
            0.848,
            0.856
          ],
          "content": "As we compare numbers using ‘=’, ‘<’ and ‘>’ signs, we can also compare expressions. We compare expressions based on their values and write the ‘equal $\\mathrm { t o } ^ { \\flat }$ , ‘greater than’ or ‘less than’ sign accordingly. For example,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.433,
            0.859,
            0.565,
            0.877
          ],
          "content": "10+2>7+1",
          "image_source": "images/page_0_equation_15.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
